-- Tokens: the lexer's output for one module.
--
-- Token kinds are flat: every keyword and every symbol is its own kind, so no
-- token carries an ordinal that a reader must decode. Only identifiers,
-- literals and character literals use `Token.payload`.
import:
	span: Span


---
The kind of a token. Keyword kinds are named `<Word>Keyword` and symbol kinds
`<Name>Symbol`; the remaining kinds document their payload as the lexer
issues it. The builder-based parser reads the tokens after `lexed_bridge` has
rewritten them: a spelling index becomes the name's row in the builder's name
table, a literal index the literal's row, and an interpolation index the index
of its bridged interpolation.

- `IdentifierToken`: payload: the index of the identifier's spelling in the module's `Spellings`.
- `DimensionNameToken`: payload: the index of the spelling of the name written directly after `#` (as in `#N`); the span covers both. A `#` followed by anything else is a `HashSymbol`.
- `IntLiteralToken`: payload: the index of the integer's `IntegerValue` among the lexed literals.
- `FloatLiteralToken`: payload: the index of the float's `FloatValue` among the lexed literals.
- `RejectedIntegerToken`: an integer literal above the Int128 maximum; no payload. The lexer reported it (`IntegerLiteralOverflow` carries its digits), so the module is rejected and its parser only has to carry on past the token.
- `RejectedFloatToken`: a float literal that is not finite; no payload; as `RejectedIntegerToken`.
- `NormalStringToken`: payload: the index of the string's `TextValue` (its text after escapes) among the lexed literals.
- `RawStringToken`: payload: as `NormalStringToken`, the text as written.
- `InterpolatedStringToken`: payload: the index of the string's `InterpolationScan` among the lexed interpolations, whose pieces are its text pieces and hole byte ranges.
- `PipeStringToken`: payload: as `NormalStringToken`, the joined lines.
- `RawPipeStringToken`: payload: as `NormalStringToken`, the joined lines as written.
- `InterpolatedPipeStringToken`: payload: as `InterpolatedStringToken`; its text pieces join the lines.
- `CharLiteralToken`: payload: the character's codepoint.
- `DocStringToken`: payload: as `NormalStringToken`, the docstring's lines.
- `NewlineToken`: no payload.
- `IndentToken`: no payload.
- `DedentToken`: no payload.
- `EndOfFileToken`: no payload.
---
fixed union TokenKind:
	FuncKeyword
	PureKeyword
	VarKeyword
	UnionKeyword
	RecordKeyword
	VoidKeyword
	WhileKeyword
	ForKeyword
	InKeyword
	IfKeyword
	ElseKeyword
	AndKeyword
	OrKeyword
	NotKeyword
	OnKeyword
	MatchKeyword
	TrueKeyword
	FalseKeyword
	BreakKeyword
	ContinueKeyword
	DebugKeyword
	WithKeyword
	ResourceKeyword
	ForeignKeyword
	PrivateKeyword
	BuiltinKeyword
	ConcurrentKeyword
	ConcurrentlyKeyword
	DetachKeyword
	SelectKeyword
	IntoOpaqueKeyword
	FromKeyword
	FromOpaqueKeyword
	AfterKeyword
	SealedKeyword
	OpaqueKeyword
	TryKeyword
	ImportKeyword
	AsKeyword
	TraitKeyword
	ImplementsKeyword
	SelfKeyword
	TypeKeyword
	AliasKeyword
	WhereKeyword
	LeftParenSymbol
	RightParenSymbol
	LeftBracketSymbol
	RightBracketSymbol
	LeftBraceSymbol
	RightBraceSymbol
	CommaSymbol
	ColonSymbol
	DotSymbol
	DotDotSymbol
	DotDotDotSymbol
	ArrowSymbol
	FatArrowSymbol
	EqualSymbol
	QuestionEqualsSymbol
	PlusSymbol
	MinusSymbol
	StarSymbol
	SlashSymbol
	PlusEqualSymbol
	MinusEqualSymbol
	StarEqualSymbol
	SlashEqualSymbol
	UnderscoreSymbol
	PercentSymbol
	HashSymbol
	AtSymbol
	PipeSymbol
	EqualEqualSymbol
	NotEqualSymbol
	LessSymbol
	LessEqualSymbol
	GreaterSymbol
	GreaterEqualSymbol
	IdentifierToken
